; COM interfaces (--mode=objfpc, the default kind): their classes descend
; from TInterfacedObject, COM and CORBA interfaces do not mix, and COM
; interfaces (reference counted) cannot be in variant parts, files or
; record results. is/as take a COM interface on the left (its object).
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/com/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:6:27: error: class 'TPlain' implements the COM interface 'IA', so it must descend from TInterfacedObject
; CHECK: errors.pas:13:24: error: a CORBA interface cannot inherit from the COM interface 'IA'
; CHECK: errors.pas:16:26: error: a COM interface cannot inherit from the CORBA interface 'IC'
; CHECK: errors.pas:20:11: error: a variant part cannot contain COM interfaces
; CHECK: errors.pas:23:19: error: the components of a file cannot be COM interfaces
; CHECK: errors.pas:30:15: error: a function cannot return a record containing COM interfaces
; CHECK: errors.pas:39:8: error: invalid operands to 'is' ('IC' and 'TObject')
; CHECK-NOT: error

; The parse tree marks COM interfaces.
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc --emit-parse-tree %S/Inputs/com/errors.pas | FileCheck --check-prefix=TREE %s
; TREE:      TypeDecl 'ia' <3:3>
; TREE-NEXT:   InterfaceTypeSpec com <3:8>
; TREE:      TypeDecl 'ic' <10:3>
; TREE-NEXT:   InterfaceTypeSpec <10:8>

; An interface type needs a name (it used to crash code generation).
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/com/anonymous.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANON %s
; ANON: anonymous.pas:2:8: error: an interface type must be declared in a 'type' section
; ANON: anonymous.pas:3:21: error: an interface type must be declared in a 'type' section
; ANON-NOT: error
